// SELF_TEST: learner practice, never timed. FINAL: the formal assessment of
// its lesson/module, optionally timed. Orthogonal to the quiz's scope/level.
//
// QUALIFYING: the odd one out — it is not learning material inside its
// lesson/topic, it is the test that lets a student SKIP that lesson/topic.
// Its scope column (lessonId or topicId) therefore names its TARGET, not its
// container, and it is excluded from progress roll-up entirely: requiring a
// student to pass the test that exempts them from a topic in order to
// complete that topic would be circular. A student qualifies by passing it
// under the quiz's own passingScore — see qualification.js.
enum QuizTag {
  SELF_TEST
  FINAL
  QUALIFYING
}

// Where one question stands within a quiz attempt. NOT_VISITED -> VISITED on
// opening it; VISITED -> ANSWERED on an answer, or -> SKIPPED on Skip. A
// SKIPPED question that is later answered becomes ANSWERED; clearing an
// answer drops it back to VISITED (or SKIPPED, if it had been skipped).
enum QuestionAttemptStatus {
  NOT_VISITED
  VISITED
  ANSWERED
  SKIPPED
}

